THIRD-PARTY DATA
----------------

This tool reads public endpoints of the Chợ Tốt marketplace (chotot.com,
gateway.chotot.com) at runtime. The terms of that service stay with Chợ Tốt and
are not granted by the licence above. The AGPL covers the code in this
repository; it says nothing about who may use the listings, asking prices, or
photographs the code fetches.

  gateway.chotot.com   Listing, category, region, seller and shop data is Chợ Tốt's
                       and its users'. This project redistributes no scraped listing
                       dataset and ships no harvested ad catalogue. The bundled
                       taxonomy files (`chotot/data/*.json`) contain only structural
                       metadata (category IDs, administrative region codes, and
                       supported facet parameters) required for client-side query
                       construction and local validation.

PRIVACY AND CONTACT DETAILS
---------------------------

Chợ Tốt seller and shop profiles often include contact telephone numbers. To protect
user privacy and comply with data minimization principles:
- The `chotot shop` and `chotot seller` commands REDACT all phone numbers by default.
- Phone numbers are only revealed when the operator explicitly passes `--show-contact`.
- The MCP server defaults to redacting phone numbers (`show_contact: false`).
- Operators must not collect, aggregate, or publish unredacted contact numbers.

RATE LIMITING AND POLITE CRAWLING
---------------------------------

The HTTP transport layer enforces rate limiting (default minimum 0.2s between
requests), exponential backoff on HTTP 429/503 responses, and respects `Retry-After`
headers. Operators must not circumvent these protections for high-volume automated
scraping.

TEST FIXTURES
-------------

`tests/fixtures/` contains mock responses and static payloads retained so parsers
and models are tested against actual gateway payload schemas. They contain sample
ad data for unit testing and are not a licence to the underlying content.
